Both reduced cell-slice solves are still running cleanly past startup; neither has hit the old crash signature. In parallel with that gate, the exact support census shows why the simple D25 factorization breaks: all 52 lower variables enter the 92-column coefficient matrix, and no affine independent-set swap raises the generic rank above 44, so the remaining eight compatibility conditions are real rather than an artifact of the tail cutoff.
