A stronger residual chart has emerged. By choosing the pivot minor entrywise, I can keep 49 of the 52 lower-tail variables completely out of a rank-44 pivot block; only three lower variables need fixing to make that block numeric and invertible. This converts the representative cell to eight residual equations in 49 variables, with the remaining 44 high pivots reconstructed linearly—far smaller and much less specialized than the 14-variable zero-tail test.
